{title: 366 - O Where Are the Reapers?}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Church}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D]O [G]where are the reapers that garner in
[G]The sheaves [F#dim]of the good [Bm/F#]from the [G]fields [C/G]of [G]sin?
[G]With sickles of truth must the [C/G]work be done,
[C/G]And [G]no one may rest [Am]till the [Em/B]“harvest [G]home.”

Refrain:
[D]Where are the reapers? O [G/D]who [D]will [G/D]come
[G/D]And [D7]share in the glory of the "harvest home"?
[D7/F#]O [G]who will help us to [C/G]garner in
[C/G]The sheaves [G]of good [Am]from the [Em/B]fields [D/A]of [G]sin?

Verse 2:
[D]The fields [G]all are ripening, and far [C/G]and [G]wide
[G]The [F#dim]world now is waiting [Bm/F#]the [G]harvest tide:
[G]But reapers are few, and the [C/G]work is great,
[C/G]And [G]much will be lost [Am]should the [Em/B]harvest [G]wait.

Verse 3:
[D]So [G]come with your sickles, ye sons [C/G]of [G]men,
[G]And [F#dim]gather together [Bm/F#]the [G]golden grain;
[G]Toil on till the Lord of the [C/G]harvest come,
[C/G]Then [G]share ye His joy [Am]in the [Em/B]"harvest [G]home."
